1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,305
<font color="#000000">As deep generative models grow more capable,</font>

2
00:00:03,385 --> 00:00:07,305
<font color="#000000">they increasingly memorize and reproduce their
training data,</font>

3
00:00:07,385 --> 00:00:10,386
<font color="#000000">raising serious privacy and copyright concerns.</font>

4
00:00:10,466 --> 00:00:13,993
<font color="#000000">This paper, from Layer 6 AI and published at ICLR 2025,</font>

5
00:00:14,073 --> 00:00:19,697
<font color="#000000">proposes the manifold memorization hypothesis: a
geometric framework that reasons about</font>

6
00:00:19,777 --> 00:00:25,139
<font color="#000000">memorization through the local intrinsic dimension
of the data and model manifolds.</font>

7
00:00:25,219 --> 00:00:29,270
<font color="#000000">It provides a formal standard for how memorized a
datapoint is,</font>

8
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:35,630
<font color="#000000">cleanly separates memorization caused by
overfitting from memorization caused by the data itself,</font>

9
00:00:35,710 --> 00:00:41,990
<font color="#000000">and yields scalable tools to detect and mitigate
memorization all the way up to Stable Diffusion.</font>

10
00:00:42,370 --> 00:00:45,717
<font color="#000000">Generative models, and diffusion models in particular,</font>

11
00:00:45,797 --> 00:00:49,271
<font color="#000000">are increasingly deployed in public-facing applications,</font>

12
00:00:49,351 --> 00:00:52,634
<font color="#000000">but with enough capacity they memorize training data.</font>

13
00:00:52,714 --> 00:00:57,774
<font color="#000000">That memorization can expose private information
and reproduce copyrighted works,</font>

14
00:00:57,854 --> 00:01:00,503
<font color="#000000">exposing model builders to legal liability.</font>

15
00:01:00,583 --> 00:01:07,928
<font color="#000000">The trouble is that the community has lacked a
single formal framework to say precisely how memorized a datapoint is.</font>

16
00:01:08,008 --> 00:01:12,815
<font color="#000000">Past definitions lean on distance to a nearest
training image in pixel space,</font>

17
00:01:12,895 --> 00:01:18,399
<font color="#000000">which fails to capture subtler forms of
memorization and cannot be computed at the scale</font>

18
00:01:18,479 --> 00:01:20,430
<font color="#000000">of models like Stable Diffusion.</font>

19
00:01:20,810 --> 00:01:28,535
<font color="#000000">The manifold hypothesis says realistic data lives
on a low-dimensional manifold embedded in a high-dimensional space.</font>

20
00:01:28,615 --> 00:01:33,871
<font color="#000000">The authors argue that this geometry is exactly the
right lens for memorization.</font>

21
00:01:33,951 --> 00:01:40,075
<font color="#000000">Purely probabilistic frameworks demand the whole
training dataset and enormous sample counts,</font>

22
00:01:40,155 --> 00:01:42,276
<font color="#000000">which is hopeless at LAION scale.</font>

23
00:01:42,356 --> 00:01:46,879
<font color="#000000">A geometric framing, by contrast, connects
memorization to a quantity</font>

24
00:01:46,959 --> 00:01:51,615
<font color="#000000">local intrinsic dimension for which practical
estimators already exist,</font>

25
00:01:51,695 --> 00:01:53,750
<font color="#000000">even for large diffusion models.</font>

26
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:58,161
<font color="#FFFFFF">The central quantity is local intrinsic dimension,</font>

27
00:01:58,241 --> 00:02:02,272
<font color="#FFFFFF">the number of degrees of freedom a datapoint has on
its manifold.</font>

28
00:02:02,352 --> 00:02:06,384
<font color="#FFFFFF">A perfectly reproduced training image sits on a
zero-dimensional manifold</font>

29
00:02:06,464 --> 00:02:10,495
<font color="#FFFFFF">a point mass.</font>

30
00:02:10,575 --> 00:02:14,606
<font color="#FFFFFF">The manifold memorization hypothesis compares the
model's local dimension to the ground truth's.</font>

31
00:02:14,686 --> 00:02:18,718
<font color="#FFFFFF">When the model's manifold is too constrained
relative to the truth,</font>

32
00:02:18,798 --> 00:02:22,829
<font color="#FFFFFF">that is overfitting-driven memorization, a genuine
modelling failure.</font>

33
00:02:22,909 --> 00:02:26,940
<font color="#FFFFFF">When the local dimension is intrinsically small
even for a correct model</font>

34
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:31,051
<font color="#FFFFFF">think of a highly specific prompt like the title of
a famous artwork</font>

35
00:02:31,131 --> 00:02:35,163
<font color="#FFFFFF">that is data-driven memorization,</font>

36
00:02:35,243 --> 00:02:39,274
<font color="#FFFFFF">which cannot be caught by comparing train and test
likelihoods.</font>

37
00:02:39,354 --> 00:02:43,385
<font color="#FFFFFF">Because true LID cannot be estimated at Stable
Diffusion scale,</font>

38
00:02:43,465 --> 00:02:47,496
<font color="#FFFFFF">the authors use three practical proxies for the
model's LID: an unconditional estimate from the FLIPD algorithm,</font>

39
00:02:47,576 --> 00:02:51,608
<font color="#FFFFFF">a conditional estimate, and the classifier-free
guidance vector norm.</font>

40
00:02:51,688 --> 00:02:55,719
<font color="#FFFFFF">They also prove that conditioning on a prompt can
only reduce local dimension,</font>

41
00:02:55,799 --> 00:02:59,830
<font color="#FFFFFF">explaining why specific prompts drive memorization.</font>

42
00:03:00,210 --> 00:03:03,838
<font color="#000000">The experiments deliberately sweep across scales.</font>

43
00:03:03,918 --> 00:03:05,124
<font color="#000000">At the small end,</font>

44
00:03:05,204 --> 00:03:13,146
<font color="#000000">two-dimensional synthetic von Mises mixtures let
the authors compute ground-truth local dimension exactly.</font>

45
00:03:13,226 --> 00:03:18,367
<font color="#000000">In the middle, StyleGAN2-ADA and an iDDPM diffusion
model on CIFAR10.</font>

46
00:03:18,447 --> 00:03:21,924
<font color="#000000">At the large end, Stable Diffusion version 1.5,</font>

47
00:03:22,004 --> 00:03:28,431
<font color="#000000">where they study 86 verbatim-memorized LAION images
against thousands of non-memorized</font>

48
00:03:28,511 --> 00:03:31,080
<font color="#000000">images drawn from LAION Aesthetics,</font>

49
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:33,350
<font color="#000000">COCO, and the Tuxemon dataset.</font>

50
00:03:33,730 --> 00:03:41,224
<font color="#000000">The headline empirical finding is that local
intrinsic dimension tracks memorization everywhere the authors look,</font>

51
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:43,704
<font color="#000000">from toy 2D data to Stable Diffusion.</font>

52
00:03:43,784 --> 00:03:50,072
<font color="#000000">Memorized images reliably get low LID estimates and
high classifier-free guidance vector norms.</font>

53
00:03:50,152 --> 00:03:51,345
<font color="#000000">Even more striking,</font>

54
00:03:51,425 --> 00:03:58,115
<font color="#000000">the unconditional LID estimate flags memorized
training images without needing their captions at all.</font>

55
00:03:58,195 --> 00:04:03,075
<font color="#000000">That is a genuinely new capability, because the
previous state of the art,</font>

56
00:04:03,155 --> 00:04:07,030
<font color="#000000">the CFG vector norm, depends on having the caption
in hand.</font>

57
00:04:07,410 --> 00:04:08,948
<font color="#000000">To mitigate memorization,</font>

58
00:04:09,028 --> 00:04:14,189
<font color="#000000">the method attributes it to specific prompt tokens
and rephrases them with GPT-4.</font>

59
00:04:14,269 --> 00:04:19,819
<font color="#000000">Ablating the number of perturbed tokens shows a
clean trade-off: perturbing more tokens</font>

60
00:04:19,899 --> 00:04:22,860
<font color="#000000">reduces memorization but also reduces fidelity.</font>

61
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:27,584
<font color="#000000">Importantly, choosing tokens by attribution beats
choosing them at random</font>

62
00:04:27,664 --> 00:04:34,184
<font color="#000000">attribution-based selection reaches lower
training-image similarity while keeping a higher CLIP score.</font>

63
00:04:34,264 --> 00:04:41,820
<font color="#000000">New attribution metrics built on the score norm and
on FLIPD work about as well as the original guidance-based metric.</font>

64
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:46,527
<font color="#000000">The single idea to walk away with is that
memorization is geometric.</font>

65
00:04:46,607 --> 00:04:51,000
<font color="#000000">If the model's local intrinsic dimension around a
point is too small,</font>

66
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,490
<font color="#000000">that point is memorized</font>

67
00:04:52,570 --> 00:04:57,935
<font color="#000000">and this holds whether the cause is overfitting or
the data being inherently simple.</font>

68
00:04:58,015 --> 00:05:01,824
<font color="#000000">Because local intrinsic dimension can be estimated
at scale,</font>

69
00:05:01,904 --> 00:05:06,101
<font color="#000000">you can both detect memorized images, even without
their captions,</font>

70
00:05:06,181 --> 00:05:11,481
<font color="#000000">and mitigate memorization by steering generation
toward higher-dimensional regions.</font>

71
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:14,786
<font color="#000000">The manifold memorization hypothesis turns a fuzzy,</font>

72
00:05:14,866 --> 00:05:18,740
<font color="#000000">much-debated phenomenon into a measurable geometric
quantity.</font>
